{{Short description|Election in Indonesia}}
{{Orphan|date=October 2025}}

The '''2024 Indonesian presidential debate''' is a series of [[debate]]s attended by three presidential candidates, [[Anies Baswedan]], [[Prabowo Subianto]], and [[Ganjar Pranowo]], as well as their vice-presidential candidates in [[2024 Indonesian presidential election]].

== Background ==
During the time frame established by the [[General Elections Commission|General Election Commission]] (KPU), presidential and vice presidential candidates use [[debate]]s as a [[Political campaign|campaign tactic]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Humas KPU |date=2023-11-29 |title=KPU Siap Gelar Debat Capres 3 Kali dan Cawapres 2 Kali |url=https://www.kpu.go.id/berita/baca/12125/kpu-siap-gelar-debat-capres-3-kali-dan-cawapres-2-kali |access-date=12 December 2023 |website=KPU 21}}</ref> Five debates between presidential and vice-presidential pairings was place throughout the campaign season in compliance with the [[Indonesian electoral law of 2017]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Farisa |first=Fitria Chusna |date=2023-11-28 |title=Aturan Debat Pilpres 2024: Pelaksanaan dan Materi Halaman all |url=https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2023/11/28/17113731/aturan-debat-pilpres-2024-pelaksanaan-dan-materi |access-date=12 December 2023 |website=KOMPAS.com |language=id}}</ref> While all three pairs of candidates will participate together in each debate, the KPU has planned three debates for presidential candidates and two for vice presidential candidates for the 2024 elections.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wibawana |first=Widhia Arum |title=Aturan Debat Pilpres 2023: Tata Penyelenggaraan hingga Materinya |url=https://news.detik.com/pemilu/d-7061255/aturan-debat-pilpres-2023-tata-penyelenggaraan-hingga-materinya |access-date=12 December 2023 |website=detiknews |language=id-ID}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-11-30 |title=Pemilu 2024: Debat capres 2024 - Apa saja yang diketahui sejauh ini? |url=https://www.bbc.com/indonesia/articles/cd1p55d1lz7o |access-date=12 December 2023 |website=BBC News Indonesia |language=id}}</ref> In contrast, during the 2019 election campaign, there were two special debates for presidential candidates, one for the vice president, and two for presidential-vice-presidential couples.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Aprilia |first=Zefanya |title=Ini Beda Format Debat Capres-Cawapres Saat Ini dengan di 2019 - Semua Halaman |url=https://www.cnbcindonesia.com/news/20231202184759-4-494038/ini-beda-format-debat-capres-cawapres-saat-ini-dengan-di-2019 |access-date=12 December 2023 |website=CNBC Indonesia |language=id-ID}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Format Debat Capres-Cawapres RI dari Masa ke Masa, Sejak 2004-Sekarang |url=https://nu.or.id/nasional/format-debat-capres-cawapres-ri-dari-masa-ke-masa-sejak-2004-sekarang-ISmMZ |access-date=12 December 2023 |website=NU Online |language=id-id}}</ref> This format modification was seen advantageous for some pairings, and it became a topic of discussion among the public and the success teams of candidate pairs.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Rosana |first=Francisca Christy |date=2023-12-10 |title=Gimik Calon Presiden dalam Debat untuk Menggaet Pemilih Muda |url=https://majalah.tempo.co/read/laporan-utama/170367/gimik-debat-calon-presiden |access-date=12 December 2023 |website=Tempo |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Liputan6.com |date=2023-12-02 |title=KPU Bantah Hilangkan Format Debat Antar Cawapres di Pilpres 2024 |url=https://www.liputan6.com/pemilu/read/5470328/kpu-bantah-hilangkan-format-debat-antar-cawapres-di-pilpres-2024 |access-date=12 December 2023 |website=liputan6.com |language=id}}</ref>

Compared to the debates held throughout the 2019 election campaign, the format of each debate's segments has not altered much. The discussion will be broken up into six sections, with a total duration of around 120 minutes. Following the presentation of the candidate couples' mission and vision in the first segment, there will follow two question and answer sessions aimed at refining the vision and mission through prepared panelist questions. The presidential candidates exchange questions and answers in the following two segments, and the sixth section concludes with a closing statement.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-12-12 |title=Debat capres 2024: Janji capres 2024 apa saja? |url=https://www.bbc.com/indonesia/articles/c1w2e29259zo |access-date=12 December 2023 |website=BBC News Indonesia |language=id}}</ref>

