The second presidential and vice presidential debate took place on December 22, 2023, at the [[Jakarta Convention Center]], Jakarta. With a modified town-hall meeting concept,<ref>{{Cite news |last=developer |first=medcom id |date=2023-12-18 |title=Update Debat Kedua Pilpres: Lokasi, Format Baru, hingga Daftar Panelis |url=https://www.medcom.id/pemilu/news-pemilu/wkBBDP4k-update-debat-kedua-pilpres-lokasi-format-baru-hingga-daftar-panelis |access-date=18 December 2023 |language=id}}</ref> this debate will be followed by the vice-presidential candidates with a discussion format similar to the previous debate. The themes of this debate are Economy, People's Economy, Digital Economy, Finance, Tax Investment, Trade, Management of State Budget and Regional Budget, Infrastructure and Cities. [[Detik.com]] editor-in-chief and [[CNN Indonesia]] host Alfito Deannova and [[Kompas TV]] host Liviana Cherlisa were appointed as moderators for the second debate.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Media |first=Kompas Cyber |date=2023-12-18 |title=Alfito Deannova dan Liviana Cherlisa Jadi Moderator Debat Cawapres Perdana Halaman all |url=https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2023/12/18/18273021/alfito-deannova-dan-liviana-cherlisa-jadi-moderator-debat-cawapres-perdana |access-date=18 December 2023 |language=id}}</ref>

Indonesian Presidential and Vice-Presidential Candidates number 1 Anies Baswedan and [[Muhaimin Iskandar]] were dressed in the same attire as the first debate, which was white shirts with black suits. They also wore accessories, including pins labeled AMIN and [[Songkok|kopiah]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Abdurrahman |first=Sultan |date=2023-12-22 |title=Pakaian Anies-Muhaimin di Debat Kedua Sama dengan Saat Debat Pertama |url=https://nasional.tempo.co/read/1812730/pakaian-anies-muhaimin-di-debat-kedua-sama-dengan-saat-debat-pertama |access-date=23 December 2023 |work=Tempo News |language=id}}</ref> Likewise, candidate pair number 2 Prabowo Subianto and [[Gibran Rakabuming Raka]] who appeared in the same outfit from the first debate, a blue shirt typical of their partner's color. Gibran rolled up his sleeves to around the elbow, while Prabowo left his sleeves up to his wrist.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Santosa |first=Lia Wanadriani |date=2023-12-22 |title=Baju adat hingga jas jadi pilihan para cawapres pada debat kedua |url=https://www.antaranews.com/berita/3883950/baju-adat-hingga-jas-jadi-pilihan-para-cawapres-pada-debat-kedua |access-date=23 December 2023 |work=Antara News |language=id}}</ref> Also, candidate number 3 Ganjar Pranowo and [[Mahfud MD]] came dressed in traditional Indonesian attire. Mahfud wore a traditional Madurese traditional outfit from [[East Java]] province, while Ganjar was also dressed in a traditional Rote outfit from [[East Nusa Tenggara]] province. In addition, their supporters also came wearing traditional clothing from different regions throughout Indonesia to watch the second debate in person.<ref name="pakaianadatpaslon3didebatkedua">{{Cite news |last=Indonesia |first=C.N.N. |title=Ganjar dan Mahfud Pakai Baju Adat NTT-Madura Hadiri Debat Cawapres |url=https://www.cnnindonesia.com/nasional/20231222185922-617-1040808/ganjar-dan-mahfud-pakai-baju-adat-ntt-madura-hadiri-debat-cawapres |language=id}}</ref> This time the debate was between vice presidential candidates Muhaimin Iskandar, Gibran Rakabuming Raka and Mahfud MD. In this second debate, the vice-presidential candidates debated on the big topic of economic issues. In the middle of the debate, Gibran Rakabuming Raka asked questions about abbreviations that other candidate did not understand, so the KPU issued a rule in the next debate, participants are prohibited using questions containing terms, abbreviations or acronyms that are not common and not understood by other participants unless they explain it first.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Putra |first=Nanda Perdana |date=5 January 2024 |title=KPU Larang Capres Pakai Pertanyaan Singkatan Tanpa Penjelasan Saat Debat |url=https://www.liputan6.com/pemilu/read/5498301/kpu-larang-capres-pakai-pertanyaan-singkatan-tanpa-penjelasan-saat-debat?page=2 |access-date=7 January 2024 |work=Liputan 6 News |language=id}}</ref>

